      "relation": "conceptually_related_to",
      "description": "Three interconnected bugs form a systemic gap: verifier trusts text output (Issue 3), executors produce reports not code due to oversize tasks (Issue 4), and no automated post-execution artifact check exists (Issue 5). Together these allow the system to PASS verification with 0 files created.",
      "source_file": "HANDOFF.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "hyper-model-routing-fragility",
      "label": "Model Routing Fragility",
      "nodes": [
        "bug-issue1-routing-fights-planner",
        "bug-issue2-intake-overrides-model",
        "bug-issue7-pt-regex-false-match"
      ],
      "relation": "conceptually_related_to",
      "description": "Three bugs in the model routing subsystem: routing check uses agent-name not phase (Issue 1), intake normalizer applies first-found alias and never overrides with more specific role-model pairings (Issue 2), and the GPT-5.5 regex has false-match risk with 'PT 5.5' text (Issue 7). The routing layer is fragile to both natural planner behavior and user intent.",
      "source_file": "HANDOFF.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "hyper-enametoolong-fix-chain",
      "label": "ENAMETOOLONG Fix Chain",
      "nodes": [
